From 7d9a21cfbe833081d4dc30934024b2a9b776fec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:27:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rkisp2: Add the ISPP parameters path

The RV1126 ISPP post-processor behind the ISP takes its module
parameters (temporal noise reduction, noise reduction, sharpening, FEC
motion mesh, ORB feature detection) through its own extensible params
node. Add a second params buffer kind to the IPA interface, filled by
the algorithms through a prepareIspp() hook alongside the ISP params,
and an Ispp algorithm that sends the modules configured in the tuning
file with every frame, each tuning dictionary naming the fields of the
UAPI block.

The imx415 tuning file lists the algorithm without modules, so the
driver's state stands until a tuning provides the tables.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
